From: gameOS <gameos@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] gameOS: enable MMC support in SPL for SD-card boot

The quartz64-a base defconfig only enables SPI loading in SPL. The
RG DS Plus has no SPI flash and no eMMC: SPL must read U-Boot proper
(u-boot.itb, raw sector 0x4000) from the microSD card itself.

SPL_DM_MMC defaults to y, the dw-mmc/sdhci Rockchip drivers are already
enabled for U-Boot proper (their Makefile entries are not phase-gated),
and SPL_SYS_MMCSD_RAW_MODE + SYS_MMCSD_RAW_MODE_U_BOOT_SECTOR=0x4000
default correctly for ARCH_ROCKCHIP. The only missing symbol is SPL_MMC,
which gates common/spl/spl_mmc.c (the BOOT_DEVICE_MMC1 loader).

Without it SPL reports "Unsupported Boot Device" and the board never
leaves SPL -- exactly the black-screen failure mode gameOS must avoid.

diff --git a/configs/quartz64-a-rk3566_defconfig b/configs/quartz64-a-rk3566_defconfig
--- a/configs/quartz64-a-rk3566_defconfig
+++ b/configs/quartz64-a-rk3566_defconfig
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 CONFIG_DEBUG_UART_BASE=0xFE660000
 CONFIG_DEBUG_UART_CLOCK=24000000
 CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_RK8XX_DISABLE_BOOT_ON_POWERON=y
+CONFIG_SPL_MMC=y
 CONFIG_SPL_SPI_FLASH_SUPPORT=y
 CONFIG_SPL_SPI=y
 CONFIG_PCI=y
